        "document_id": "4585",
        "explanation": "Senator Schumer states that he pushed for additional funding for the Assistance to Firefighters Grant Program and that he was among the first senators to recognize the need for the program. He explicitly links the grants to his advocacy."
      }
    ],
    "negative_clarification": "Credit-claiming does NOT occur when a senator merely expresses support for a policy, critiques an opponent or administration, or describes a general legislative process without tying it to their personal actions. Statements of concern, policy positions, or descriptions of meetings or events without personal attribution do not qualify as credit-claiming.",
    "negative_examples": [
